    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS). There's a single test class, `AcceptanceTest`, and all 3 tests are green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI introduced address normalization on owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1` (which handles `POST /api/owners`).\n\n**New `normalizeAddress` method** \u2014 trims and collapses whitespace, upper-cases, then token-by-token expands the abbreviations `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`. Token-based expansion means only whole words are replaced (e.g. `EAST` is untouched). `null`/whitespace-only inputs yield `\"\"`.\n\n**Wired into the three required places:**\n1. **Store & return normalized** \u2014 `addOwner` sets `owner.setAddress(normalizeAddress(owner.getAddress()))` right after mapping, so the persisted and returned `address` is normalized (`\"  12  main  st \"` \u2192 `\"12 MAIN STREET\"`, `\"7 elm ave\"` \u2192 `\"7 ELM AVENUE\"`).\n2. **Required-field check** \u2014 `validateRequiredOwnerFields` now tests `isBlank(normalizeAddress(...))`, so an address blank after normalization is rejected with 400.\n3. **Address comparisons** \u2014 `applyHousehold` now compares both the joiner's and existing owners' addresses via `normalizeAddress`, and passes that normalized address into `generateHouseholdId`, so household duplicate detection and the shared household id both use the normalized form.\n\nI also updated the javadoc on `applyHousehold` and `normalizeHouseholdField` (now describing last-name-only) to stay accurate.",
